hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17776","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahia narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya, that he said upon the pulpit at Rhodes when he flogged the two men who had stolen the spoils of the people. He said: Nothing prevented me from cutting them except that Busr ibn Artat found a man stealing in the expedition called Masdar, so he flogged him and did not cut his hand, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from cutting on expedition."
"17777","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us who said: Abdullah narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid informed us who said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to us, from Shuyaym ibn Baytan, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya who said: I was with Busr ibn Artat, and Masdar was brought, having stolen a Bactrian camel. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid us from cutting on expedition, I would cut you. So he was flogged, then his way was freed."
"17778","Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Maysara ibn Halbas narrated to us who said: I heard my father reporting from Busr ibn Artat al-Qurashi who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate: O Allah, make good our end in all matters, and save us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter. Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Haytham."
